 "text": "Hi, how are things with you? A simple cable cage works well, and it' easy to reach. Some desks have a secret hole for pulling cables out through. No problem. A simple cable cage works well, and it' easy to reach. Some desks have a secret hole for pulling cables out through. Then start by pulling it out far from the edge. Then wrap the longer sides around a little loop, and tape them together. Give each monitor its own cable, so you' not tying a knot with the monitor cable. And loop them around the back of the desk, out of sight.",
